.TH HIRO.CONF 5 "August 2026" "HIRO" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
hiro.conf \- HIRO daemon configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/hiro/config.toml
.SH DESCRIPTION
TOML configuration for \fBhirod\fR(8). Every key is optional; missing
values fall back to the built-in defaults (see
.I /etc/hiro/config.toml.example
for the complete set with documentation).
.SH SECTIONS
.TP
.B [device]
Camera node selection (\fIpath\fR), IR-only enforcement (\fIrequire_ir\fR),
emitter mode, stream warm-up period.
.TP
.B [camera]
Capture geometry: \fIwidth\fR, \fIheight\fR, \fIfps\fR, \fIpixel_format\fR
(YUYV recommended), \fImax_frames\fR per attempt.
.TP
.B [recognition]
Model directory, detector/embedder names, match threshold, quorum, timeout,
liveness thresholds, and enrollment quality gates (face size, sharpness,
pose dedupe, and the optional enrollment variance gate
\fIenroll_min_variance\fR, which defaults to off so users can hold still
while templates are captured). Automatic per-user match-threshold
calibration (\fIauto_threshold\fR, default true): enrollment measures the
user's genuine scores and stores a per-user threshold (bounded by
\fIauto_threshold_min\fR/\fIauto_threshold_max\fR, a margin
\fIauto_threshold_margin\fR below the measured low end), and every
successful match slowly adapts it toward the observed score at the EMA rate
\fIauto_threshold_adapt\fR (0 disables tracking; adaptation never runs on
failures). Set \fIauto_threshold = false\fR to rely on the global
\fImatch_threshold\fR alone.
.TP
.B [security]
Rate limiting, lockout, per-user template limit, camera-pinning policy, the
after-reboot password gate (\fIrequire_password_after_boot\fR, default
true: face auth only works for users who have logged in since the last
reboot, armed only by the root PAM session hook), and the per-user camera
budget (\fIcamera_budget_secs\fR / \fIcamera_budget_window_secs\fR,
default 15s/60s: a single account cannot monopolise the camera and block
other users' face auth).
.TP
.B [storage]
Template database and encryption key paths.
.TP
.B [daemon]
Socket path, log level, audit toggle, maximum per-request timeout.
.TP
.B [keyring]
Automatic login-keyring unlock on face login. \fIenabled\fR defaults to
false; when true, \fIservices\fR lists the PAM services (e.g.
gdm-password) whose stacks receive the injected authtok. The password is
enrolled with \fBhiro keyring set\fR and re-verified against the account
before each release.
.TP
.B [approval]
Action-approval gate (default on): non-login services pause for an
explicit Allow/Deny decision after a confident face match.
\fIbypass_services\fR lists the user-initiated services that skip the
prompt (greeters, session logins, and \fBhiro test\fR by default).
\fItimeout_ms\fR bounds the decision window; the request is denied only
when it expires or the user clicks Deny. Stepping out of the frame is not
a failure: after \fIabsent_frames\fR consecutive frames with no convincing
face (score below the effective threshold minus
\fIabsent_score_margin\fR) the buttons disappear but the request keeps
waiting until the timeout. With \fIsecure_desktop\fR = true (default
false) the prompt is shown on a dedicated VT by \fBhiro-approve\fR
instead of the in-session indicator (\fIsecure_vt\fR, \fIsecure_dialog\fR).
.TP
.B [ui]
Desktop-agnostic session UI (\fBhiro-ui\fR). \fIactive\fR is
\fI"auto"\fR (default), \fI"on"\fR, or \fI"off"\fR. In \fIauto\fR mode
hiro-ui renders unless the \fBhiro-status@hiro\fR GNOME Shell extension
reports enabled — that probe runs against the live shell, so it does not
depend on desktop environment variables (\fIXDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP\fR and
friends are frequently missing in systemd user units). \fIon\fR forces
rendering and \fIoff\fR disables the in-session UI entirely.
.SH RELOADING
Apply changes with:
.B hiro reload
(the daemon rebuilds the pipeline when the recognition section changes).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hirod (8),
.BR hiro (1)
